@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- ca-interpretation-powers.l4
--
-- The Interpretation Act (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. I-21: the sections that give or imply a power.  Pass 2.
-- Sections 23(4), 24, 31 and 34.1.  Imports only the standard library.
--
-- THE HOUSE RULE FOR A RULE THAT HAS A STATED CONDITION.  The answer is TRUE where the text states the condition and it is met.
-- It is FALSE only where the text says "shall not be deemed", "does not include" or "means" (which gives the whole meaning), or where a
-- subsection says in terms that nothing in a paragraph authorizes a thing.
-- Where the case asked about is not one the text addresses, the answer is a refusal, never FALSE.
-- Each refusal is a named function at a generic type, so that its name says what the text leaves open.
-- Where a section creates a power, its holder and the one who is liable to it are in the `## Jural relations` table of NOTES.md.

§ `Section 23(4): remuneration`

-- Plain gloss: where a person is appointed to an office, the appointing authority may fix, vary or terminate that person's remuneration.
DECLARE `What an appointing authority may do about remuneration` IS ONE OF
    `fix it`
    `vary it`
    `terminate it`
    `something else`

-- src:186 | (4) Where a person is appointed to an office, the appointing authority may fix, vary or terminate that person’s remuneration.
@ref Interpretation Act s 23(4) (src:186)
GIVEN w IS A `What an appointing authority may do about remuneration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointing authority of an office may, as to the remuneration of the person appointed to it,` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `fix it`        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `vary it`       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `terminate it`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN `section 23(4) names three powers over remuneration and does not say whether the authority has any other`

-- src:186 | (4) Where a person is appointed to an office, the appointing authority may fix, vary or terminate that person’s remuneration.
@ref Interpretation Act s 23(4) (src:186)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 23(4) names three powers over remuneration and does not say whether the authority has any other` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 23(4) names three powers over remuneration and does not say whether the authority has any other"

§ `Section 24: powers that words imply`

-- Plain gloss, subsection (1): words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include, in the
-- discretion of the authority in whom the power of appointment is vested, the power to terminate the appointment or remove or suspend the
-- officer, to re-appoint or reinstate the officer, and to appoint another person in the officer's stead or to act in the officer's stead.
DECLARE `A power that words authorizing an appointment during pleasure include` IS ONE OF
    `terminate the appointment`
    `remove the public officer`
    `suspend the public officer`
    `re-appoint the public officer`
    `reinstate the public officer`
    `appoint another person in the stead of the public officer`
    `appoint another person to act in the stead of the public officer`
    `some other power`

-- src:190 | 24 (1) Words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include, in the discretion of the authority in whom the power of appointment is vested, the power to
-- src:191 | (a) terminate the appointment or remove or suspend the public officer;
-- src:192 | (b) re-appoint or reinstate the public officer; and
-- src:193 | (c) appoint another person in the stead of, or to act in the stead of, the public officer.
@ref Interpretation Act s 24(1) (src:190-193)
GIVEN p IS A `A power that words authorizing an appointment during pleasure include`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include the power to` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `terminate the appointment`                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `remove the public officer`                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `suspend the public officer`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `re-appoint the public officer`                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reinstate the public officer`                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `appoint another person in the stead of the public officer`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `appoint another person to act in the stead of the public officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some other power` THEN `section 24 says what words include and does not say that nothing else is included`

-- Plain gloss, subsection (2): words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include a minister acting for
-- that minister (or, if the office is vacant, a minister designated by or under an order in council), the minister's successors in the
-- office, the minister's deputy, and a person appointed to serve in the department or ministry of state in a capacity appropriate to the act.
DECLARE `Who words directed to a minister include` IS ONE OF
    `a minister acting for that minister`
    `if the office is vacant, a minister designated to act in the office by or under the authority of an order in council`
    `a successor of that minister in the office`
    `the deputy of that minister, or of the successors`
    `a person appointed to serve, in the department or ministry of state over which the minister presides, in a capacity appropriate to the doing of the act or thing`
    `someone else`

-- src:195 | (2) Words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing, regardless of whether the act or thing is administrative, legislative or judicial, or otherwise applying to that minister as the holder of the office, include
-- src:196 | (a) a minister acting for that minister or, if the office is vacant, a minister designated to act in the office by or under the authority of an order in council;
-- src:197 | (b) the successors of that minister in the office;
-- src:198 | (c) his or their deputy; and
-- src:199 | (d) notwithstanding paragraph (c), a person appointed to serve, in the department or ministry of state over which the minister presides, in a capacity appropriate to the doing of the act or thing, or to the words so applying.
@ref Interpretation Act s 24(2) (src:195-199)
GIVEN w IS A `Who words directed to a minister include`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `a minister acting for that minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `if the office is vacant, a minister designated to act in the office by or under the authority of an order in council` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a successor of that minister in the office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the deputy of that minister, or of the successors` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person appointed to serve, in the department or ministry of state over which the minister presides, in a capacity appropriate to the doing of the act or thing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN `section 24 says what words include and does not say that nothing else is included`

-- Plain gloss, subsection (3): paragraph (2)(c) or (d), the deputy and the person appointed to serve, does not authorize the exercise of
-- an authority conferred on a minister to make a regulation as defined in the Statutory Instruments Act.
-- FORK F-24-DEPUTY: subsection (3) names paragraphs (2)(c) and (d) and no other provision, so it does not reach the deputy of a public
-- officer other than a minister, whom subsection (4) names.  Taken: the literal text (the deputy under (4) is not restricted by (3)); the
-- function for subsection (4) below therefore has no input about making a regulation.  The other reading carries the restriction of (3)
-- to (4)'s deputy by its evident purpose; the marginal note "Restriction as to public servants" cannot widen it (s 14: marginal notes
-- form no part of the enactment).
-- src:201 | (3) Nothing in paragraph (2)(c) or (d) shall be construed as authorizing the exercise of any authority conferred on a minister to make a regulation as defined in the Statutory Instruments Act.
@ref Interpretation Act s 24(3) (src:201)
GIVEN `the authority conferred on the minister is to make a regulation as defined in the Statutory Instruments Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph 24(2)(c) or (d) authorizes the exercise of an authority conferred on a minister, where` `the authority conferred on the minister is to make a regulation as defined in the Statutory Instruments Act` MEANS
    NOT `the authority conferred on the minister is to make a regulation as defined in the Statutory Instruments Act`

-- Plain gloss, subsection (4): words directing or empowering a public officer other than a minister to do an act or thing, or applying to
-- the officer by name of office, include the officer's successors in the office and the officer's or their deputy.
-- (FORK F-24-DEPUTY, above: no restriction on regulation-making is applied to the deputy named here.)
DECLARE `Who words directed to a public officer other than a minister include` IS ONE OF
    `a successor of the public officer in the office`
    `the deputy of the public officer, or of the successors`
    `someone else`

-- src:203 | (4) Words directing or empowering any public officer, other than a minister of the Crown, to do any act or thing, or otherwise applying to the public officer by his name of office, include his successors in the office and his or their deputy.
@ref Interpretation Act s 24(4) (src:203)
GIVEN w IS A `Who words directed to a public officer other than a minister include`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words directing or empowering a public officer other than a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing include` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `a successor of the public officer in the office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the deputy of the public officer, or of the successors` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN `section 24 says what words include and does not say that nothing else is included`

-- Plain gloss, subsection (5): where a power is conferred or a duty imposed on the holder of an office, it may be exercised, and must be
-- performed, by the person for the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office.
-- src:205 | (5) Where a power is conferred or a duty imposed on the holder of an office, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the person for the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office.
@ref Interpretation Act s 24(5) (src:205)
GIVEN `the person is for the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power conferred on the holder of an office may be exercised, and a duty imposed on the holder shall be performed, by a person who is` `the person is for the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person is for the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 24(5) says who may exercise the power and perform the duty and does not say that no one else may`

-- src:190 | 24 (1) Words authorizing the appointment of a public officer to hold office during pleasure include, in the discretion of the authority in whom the power of appointment is vested, the power to
-- src:191 | (a) terminate the appointment or remove or suspend the public officer;
-- src:192 | (b) re-appoint or reinstate the public officer; and
-- src:193 | (c) appoint another person in the stead of, or to act in the stead of, the public officer.
-- src:194 | Power to act for ministers
-- src:195 | (2) Words directing or empowering a minister of the Crown to do an act or thing, regardless of whether the act or thing is administrative, legislative or judicial, or otherwise applying to that minister as the holder of the office, include
-- src:196 | (a) a minister acting for that minister or, if the office is vacant, a minister designated to act in the office by or under the authority of an order in council;
-- src:197 | (b) the successors of that minister in the office;
-- src:198 | (c) his or their deputy; and
-- src:199 | (d) notwithstanding paragraph (c), a person appointed to serve, in the department or ministry of state over which the minister presides, in a capacity appropriate to the doing of the act or thing, or to the words so applying.
-- src:200 | Restriction as to public servants
-- src:201 | (3) Nothing in paragraph (2)(c) or (d) shall be construed as authorizing the exercise of any authority conferred on a minister to make a regulation as defined in the Statutory Instruments Act.
-- src:202 | Successors to and deputy of public officer
-- src:203 | (4) Words directing or empowering any public officer, other than a minister of the Crown, to do any act or thing, or otherwise applying to the public officer by his name of office, include his successors in the office and his or their deputy.
-- src:204 | Powers of holder of public office
-- src:205 | (5) Where a power is conferred or a duty imposed on the holder of an office, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the person for the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office.
@ref Interpretation Act s 24 (src:190-205)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 24 says what words include and does not say that nothing else is included` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 24 says what words include and does not say that nothing else is included"

-- src:205 | (5) Where a power is conferred or a duty imposed on the holder of an office, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the person for the time being charged with the execution of the powers and duties of the office.
@ref Interpretation Act s 24(5) (src:205)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 24(5) says who may exercise the power and perform the duty and does not say that no one else may` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 24(5) says who may exercise the power and perform the duty and does not say that no one else may"

§ `Section 31: miscellaneous rules about powers`

-- Plain gloss, subsection (1): where a thing is required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, provincial court judge, justice of the
-- peace or any functionary or officer, it is done by or before one whose jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where it is to be done.
-- src:238 | 31 (1) Where anything is required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, provincial court judge, justice of the peace or any functionary or officer, it shall be done by or before one whose jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(1) (src:238)
GIVEN `the jurisdiction or powers of the one by or before whom it is done extend to the place where the thing is to be done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a thing required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, justice of the peace, functionary or officer is done as section 31(1) requires, where` `the jurisdiction or powers of the one by or before whom it is done extend to the place where the thing is to be done` MEANS
    `the jurisdiction or powers of the one by or before whom it is done extend to the place where the thing is to be done`

-- Plain gloss, subsection (2): where power is given to a person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing, the
-- powers necessary to enable that to be done are deemed also given.
-- src:240 | (2) Where power is given to a person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of any act or thing, all such powers as are necessary to enable the person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing are deemed to be also given.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(2) (src:240)
GIVEN `the power is necessary to enable the person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power is deemed also given to a person, officer or functionary who is given power to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing, where` `the power is necessary to enable the person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the power is necessary to enable the person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 31(2) deems the necessary powers also given and does not say whether a power that is not necessary is`

-- src:240 | (2) Where power is given to a person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of any act or thing, all such powers as are necessary to enable the person, officer or functionary to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing are deemed to be also given.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(2) (src:240)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 31(2) deems the necessary powers also given and does not say whether a power that is not necessary is` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 31(2) deems the necessary powers also given and does not say whether a power that is not necessary is"

-- Plain gloss, subsection (3): where a power is conferred or a duty imposed, the power may be exercised and the duty performed from time to
-- time as occasion requires.
DECLARE `A power conferred or a duty imposed` IS ONE OF
    `a power conferred`
    `a duty imposed`

-- src:242 | (3) Where a power is conferred or a duty imposed, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(3) (src:242)
GIVEN k IS A `A power conferred or a duty imposed`
      `occasion requires it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`from time to time, as occasion requires, it is open to exercise or perform` k `where` `occasion requires it` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a power conferred` THEN BRANCH IF `occasion requires it` THEN TRUE OTHERWISE `section 31(3) speaks of exercising and performing as occasion requires and says nothing of a time when it does not`
    WHEN `a duty imposed`    THEN BRANCH IF `occasion requires it` THEN TRUE OTHERWISE `section 31(3) speaks of exercising and performing as occasion requires and says nothing of a time when it does not`

-- src:242 | (3) Where a power is conferred or a duty imposed, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(3) (src:242)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 31(3) speaks of exercising and performing as occasion requires and says nothing of a time when it does not` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 31(3) speaks of exercising and performing as occasion requires and says nothing of a time when it does not"

-- Plain gloss, subsection (4): a power to make regulations is construed as including a power to repeal, amend or vary the regulations and
-- make others, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any.
DECLARE `What a power to make regulations includes` IS ONE OF
    `repeal the regulations`
    `amend the regulations`
    `vary the regulations`
    `make other regulations`
    `something else`

-- src:244 | (4) Where a power is conferred to make regulations, the power shall be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, amend or vary the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(4) (src:244)
GIVEN w IS A `What a power to make regulations includes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power to make regulations is construed as including a power to` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `repeal the regulations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `amend the regulations`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `vary the regulations`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `make other regulations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN `section 31(4) says what the power includes and does not say that nothing else is included`

-- src:244 | (4) Where a power is conferred to make regulations, the power shall be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, amend or vary the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(4) (src:244)
GIVEN `it is exercised in the same manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is subject to the same consent and conditions, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the included power is the one section 31(4) describes where` `it is exercised in the same manner` `and` `it is subject to the same consent and conditions, if any` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is exercised in the same manner` AND `it is subject to the same consent and conditions, if any` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 31(4) describes a power exercisable in the same manner and on the same conditions and says nothing of one that is not`

-- src:244 | (4) Where a power is conferred to make regulations, the power shall be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, amend or vary the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(4) (src:244)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 31(4) says what the power includes and does not say that nothing else is included` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 31(4) says what the power includes and does not say that nothing else is included"

-- src:244 | (4) Where a power is conferred to make regulations, the power shall be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, amend or vary the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act s 31(4) (src:244)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 31(4) describes a power exercisable in the same manner and on the same conditions and says nothing of one that is not` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 31(4) describes a power exercisable in the same manner and on the same conditions and says nothing of one that is not"

§ `Section 34.1: entering a dwelling-house to arrest`

-- Plain gloss: a person who may issue a warrant to arrest or apprehend a person under an Act of Parliament other than the Criminal Code has,
-- on the same terms and conditions, the powers a judge or justice has under the Criminal Code to authorize (a) entry into the dwelling-house
-- described in the warrant to arrest or apprehend the person, if the person issuing it is satisfied by information on oath that there are
-- reasonable grounds to believe the person is or will be present there, and (b) entry without prior announcement, if the requirement of
-- subsection 529.4(1) of the Criminal Code is met.
-- src:270 | (a) to authorize the entry into a dwelling-house described in the warrant for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person, if the person issuing the warrant is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person is or will be present in the dwelling-house; and
@ref Interpretation Act s 34.1(a) (src:270)
GIVEN `the warrant is to arrest or apprehend a person under an Act of Parliament other than the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person issuing the warrant is satisfied by information on oath` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is or will be present in the dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house described in it where` `the warrant is to arrest or apprehend a person under an Act of Parliament other than the Criminal Code` `and` `the person issuing the warrant is satisfied by information on oath` `that` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is or will be present in the dwelling-house` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the warrant is to arrest or apprehend a person under an Act of Parliament other than the Criminal Code`
              AND `the person issuing the warrant is satisfied by information on oath`
              AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested is or will be present in the dwelling-house`
        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `section 34.1 gives the power on the conditions it states and says nothing of the case where they are not met`

-- src:271 | (b) to authorize the entry into the dwelling-house without prior announcement if the requirement of subsection 529.4(1) of the Criminal Code is met.
@ref Interpretation Act s 34.1(b) (src:271)
GIVEN `the warrant is to arrest or apprehend a person under an Act of Parliament other than the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement of subsection 529.4(1) of the Criminal Code is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person issuing a warrant may authorize entry into the dwelling-house without prior announcement where` `the warrant is to arrest or apprehend a person under an Act of Parliament other than the Criminal Code` `and` `the requirement of subsection 529.4(1) of the Criminal Code is met` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the warrant is to arrest or apprehend a person under an Act of Parliament other than the Criminal Code`
              AND `the requirement of subsection 529.4(1) of the Criminal Code is met`
        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `section 34.1 gives the power on the conditions it states and says nothing of the case where they are not met`

-- src:269 | 34.1 Any person who may issue a warrant to arrest or apprehend a person under any Act of Parliament, other than the Criminal Code, has the same powers, subject to the same terms and conditions, as a judge or justice has under the Criminal Code
-- src:270 | (a) to authorize the entry into a dwelling-house described in the warrant for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person, if the person issuing the warrant is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person is or will be present in the dwelling-house; and
-- src:271 | (b) to authorize the entry into the dwelling-house without prior announcement if the requirement of subsection 529.4(1) of the Criminal Code is met.
@ref Interpretation Act s 34.1 (src:269-271)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 34.1 gives the power on the conditions it states and says nothing of the case where they are not met` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 34.1 gives the power on the conditions it states and says nothing of the case where they are not met"
